  {
   "text": "The three-lobe spinner is built in the open project, at 75 mm across and 14.6 mm tall, and it has not been sliced or sent to the printer.\n\n- **Spinner:** three lobes on a 37.5 mm radius, 8 mm thick, sitting 0.3 mm above the base and 0.3 mm below the top cap.\n- **Hub:** an 8.6 mm bore around the 8 mm fixed axle, so it spins without a bearing.\n- **Base and cap:** a 20 mm base disc, 3 mm thick, and a 12 mm top cap, 3 mm thick, which holds the spinner on the axle.\n\nThe part passes everything in the plan except the minimum wall, which measures 0.798 mm against 0.8 mm. That is a rounding-level miss, and the thinnest spot should still print as two walls on the 0.4 mm nozzle. I did not find the exact location of that spot.\n\nThe sizes beyond the 75 mm span are my estimates: the lobe tip width (14 mm), hub (16 mm), spinner thickness, axle, bore, print gap, base and cap. The 0.3 mm gaps are the ones most likely to need adjusting after a test print, since clearance varies by printer.\n\nNext step: I can slice it for the P1S with PLA, and I'll send it to the printer only when you ask. Saving the design file did not work from here, so it exists only in the open project for now."
